Report a cell's OOXML type and whether its number format is a date.

xlsxio reports every cell as text. Two things it knows, or could know, never
reach the caller, and without them the typed cell model in design section 13
cannot be built at all.

First, the t= attribute. data_sheet_expat_callback_find_cell_start read it
only to test for "s", and everything else fell through to value_string. A
boolean (t="b"), an error (t="e"), a formula result (t="str") and an ISO date
(t="d") were therefore indistinguishable from a number downstream. This reads
the whole vocabulary and keeps inline strings distinct as well.

Second, number formats. OOXML stores a date as an ordinary number; the format
attached through the cell's s= index is the only thing that says it is a date.
Upstream locates xl/styles.xml in main_sheet_get_rels_callback_data, and then
frees the name without ever opening the part -- stylesfile is assigned in one
place and freed in another, and read nowhere. So the information was not
merely unexposed, it was never parsed. This adds a small parser for the two
elements that matter, cellXfs and numFmts, and a lookup from a cell's style
index to "is this a date or a time".

Deciding date-ness from a format code needs care: literal text in quotes,
backslash escapes and bracketed sections must not be scanned, or the custom
format "day" 0.00 reads as a date because of the d, a and y in a string
literal. Bracketed sections are scanned only for elapsed-time codes such as
[h], which are times; [Red] and condition brackets are skipped.

The public API is extended rather than changed. No existing signature moves;
two accessors report the type and date-ness of the cell that
xlsxioread_sheet_next_cell() last returned. The callback interface hands the
caller no handle to ask, so the accessors are on the sheet handle and serve
the iterator path, which is the one zuxlsx drives. Because the type and style
are reset before the value reaches the caller, both are preserved in
last_cell_type and last_cell_style at the point of reset.

The number format table is owned by data_sheet_callback_data and destroyed in
its cleanup, alongside the shared string list, so both read paths free it
without a new call site.

Note the styles parse passes NULL for expat_process_zip_file()'s parser
out-parameter. That function frees the parser itself unless it returns early
on XML_STATUS_SUSPENDED, which only the worksheet walk asks for; taking the
pointer back and freeing it again is a double free.

Origin: written for zuxlsx. Not upstream.
Applies to xlsxio 0.2.36 with 0001 and 0002 already applied.
